1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,600
[The D Dorm]

2
00:00:02,600 --> 00:00:05,400
Honestly, I miss you every day.

3
00:00:05,420 --> 00:00:07,910
I long for you.

4
00:00:07,930 --> 00:00:12,550
Dreaming of you every single night.

5
00:00:13,110 --> 00:00:15,000
My shining moon.

6
00:00:15,020 --> 00:00:16,329
My everlasting love.

7
00:00:16,350 --> 00:00:17,960
I cannot stand it.

8
00:00:17,980 --> 00:00:20,460
I miss you, Gaysorn.

9
00:00:21,940 --> 00:00:22,970
Grandpa,

10
00:00:22,990 --> 00:00:24,090
what's wrong with you, huh?

11
00:00:24,330 --> 00:00:25,440
Well, I am disappointed!

12
00:00:26,180 --> 00:00:27,820
I thought Dew's grandmother

13
00:00:27,840 --> 00:00:30,470
was Gaysorn,
the one I missed dearly,

14
00:00:30,490 --> 00:00:32,400
but she is not.

15
00:00:33,290 --> 00:00:34,580
My heart

16
00:00:34,600 --> 00:00:36,800
is shattered.

17
00:00:37,920 --> 00:00:40,210
Sadhu. I hope Grandpa's soul

18
00:00:40,230 --> 00:00:41,880
shatters, just as he said.

19
00:00:41,910 --> 00:00:42,640
Sadhu!

20
00:00:42,660 --> 00:00:43,980
How dare you curse me like that?!

21
00:00:44,380 --> 00:00:44,780
Huh?!

22
00:00:44,800 --> 00:00:46,500
Grandpa, he's the first person we asked.

23
00:00:46,520 --> 00:00:47,480
Why are you so down?

24
00:00:48,040 --> 00:00:49,960
"The first person"?
What does that mean?

25
00:00:52,560 --> 00:00:54,190
It was "the first time," Auntie Duang.

26
00:00:54,740 --> 00:00:56,570
It's my first time
eating at your restaurant.

27
00:00:56,600 --> 00:00:58,240
I usually just order food
to eat in my room.

28
00:00:58,650 --> 00:01:00,120
Come more often, then.

29
00:01:00,220 --> 00:01:01,760
Your grandpa used to come here a lot.

30
00:01:01,860 --> 00:01:04,230
Before he died,
he said he'd lower my rent.

31
00:01:04,680 --> 00:01:05,680
Lower your rent?

32
00:01:05,700 --> 00:01:07,060
When did I say that, huh?!

33
00:01:07,080 --> 00:01:08,280
Anus Duang!

34
00:01:09,100 --> 00:01:09,690
Oh, is that so?

35
00:01:10,120 --> 00:01:12,620
But is "Anus Duang" your full name?

36
00:01:13,850 --> 00:01:14,380
Look.

37
00:01:14,400 --> 00:01:15,310
[Duangjai's Kitchen, Made-to-Order Food]

38
00:01:15,330 --> 00:01:16,210
"Duangjai."

39
00:01:16,410 --> 00:01:17,130
Wait,

40
00:01:17,150 --> 00:01:19,150
Gramps only calls me "Anus Duang."

41
00:01:19,170 --> 00:01:19,910
How did you know that?

42
00:01:20,850 --> 00:01:22,289
Oh, it was just a guess.

43
00:01:22,310 --> 00:01:24,600
You look like you've got pain in your anus.

44
00:01:24,970 --> 00:01:25,690
No!

45
00:01:25,710 --> 00:01:26,710
I'm all good now.

46
00:01:26,730 --> 00:01:28,110
- Oh, you are?!
- Yes!

47
00:01:28,130 --> 00:01:28,870
Oh, that's good news.

48
00:01:28,890 --> 00:01:30,330
But I'm not asking you to keep his promise.

49
00:01:30,350 --> 00:01:32,750
I just want to fulfill his wishes

50
00:01:32,770 --> 00:01:34,130
so he can rest in peace.

51
00:01:34,150 --> 00:01:35,860
- I see... Is that so?
- Mm.

52
00:01:35,890 --> 00:01:36,970
Hey, Mom.

53
00:01:37,390 --> 00:01:39,640
You may be my mom,
but if you're committing fraud,

54
00:01:39,789 --> 00:01:40,789
I'll arrest you.

55
00:01:40,810 --> 00:01:42,600
What fraud?!

56
00:01:42,620 --> 00:01:44,640
I was just teasing Dobby!

57
00:01:45,509 --> 00:01:46,860
Oh, teasing, huh?

58
00:01:48,500 --> 00:01:50,560
So, can you think of any tenants

59
00:01:50,580 --> 00:01:52,630
who have a relative named Gaysorn?

60
00:01:52,650 --> 00:01:53,930
Danis,

61
00:01:53,950 --> 00:01:55,840
"Auntie Duang" isn't
the Civil Registration Office, you know.

62
00:01:55,860 --> 00:01:57,020
I don't know everything.

63
00:01:57,039 --> 00:01:58,600
I only know a little.
- I see.

64
00:01:58,640 --> 00:02:00,720
I only know who they are,
where they come from,

65
00:02:00,740 --> 00:02:02,930
their partner's name,
what they do for a living, how much they make,

66
00:02:02,950 --> 00:02:04,480
and what they like to eat. That's it.

67
00:02:04,500 --> 00:02:05,930
Wow, you only know a little, huh?

68
00:02:05,950 --> 00:02:06,950
If you knew any more than this...

69
00:02:06,970 --> 00:02:08,520
would you even know
what brand of underwear they wear?

70
00:02:08,539 --> 00:02:10,139
- I do know that about some.
- Huh?!

71
00:02:11,290 --> 00:02:15,620
♫You only one, just you, the only one♫

72
00:02:15,640 --> 00:02:20,320
♫Millions around, no one's like you, baby♫

73
00:02:20,340 --> 00:02:21,360
Singing it wrong, too.

74
00:02:22,260 --> 00:02:23,590
♫Dance a little, black shirt♫

75
00:02:23,610 --> 00:02:24,920
♫Dance a little, black shirt♫

76
00:02:24,940 --> 00:02:26,130
- Hey!
- Ugh!

77
00:02:26,150 --> 00:02:27,070
You're messing with him.

78
00:02:27,090 --> 00:02:28,280
Do you even know him? He's a cop.

79
00:02:28,300 --> 00:02:29,190
- Oh, a cop?
- Mm.

80
00:02:29,210 --> 00:02:30,060
Hello.

81
00:02:30,079 --> 00:02:30,960
Uh, hello...

82
00:02:31,079 --> 00:02:32,170
Hey, you.

83
00:02:32,190 --> 00:02:33,910
What kind of weird role
are you playing this time?

84
00:02:34,000 --> 00:02:35,590
You can't call me that.

85
00:02:35,610 --> 00:02:36,610
You have to call me

86
00:02:36,980 --> 00:02:38,670
"Daisy."

87
00:02:39,610 --> 00:02:40,500
"Daisy"?

88
00:02:40,520 --> 00:02:41,900
- Daisy.
- Daisy...

89
00:02:41,930 --> 00:02:42,750
- Mama.
- Don't call me "you" again.

90
00:02:42,770 --> 00:02:43,930
- Yes, I'm sorry.
- Don't do it again.

91
00:02:43,950 --> 00:02:45,910
Oh, I want to sit down now.
I'm gonna sit down.

92
00:02:45,930 --> 00:02:46,810
Daisy?

93
00:02:46,829 --> 00:02:47,310
Hey,

94
00:02:47,329 --> 00:02:48,190
not like that.

95
00:02:48,320 --> 00:02:49,750
Say "Daisy."

96
00:02:50,150 --> 00:02:51,630
- Daisy?
- Daisy.

97
00:02:51,650 --> 00:02:53,170
- Daisy.
- Daisy.

98
00:02:53,190 --> 00:02:54,350
- Daisy. Dai...
- Daisy. Dai...

99
00:02:54,370 --> 00:02:55,660
- sy.
- Ugh!

100
00:02:55,870 --> 00:02:56,870
I know you're Daisy.

101
00:02:56,890 --> 00:02:57,950
That isn't important right now.

102
00:02:58,130 --> 00:02:58,980
Why did you drag your suitcase here?

103
00:02:59,000 --> 00:02:59,710
Oh,

104
00:02:59,730 --> 00:03:00,830
I'm staying with you tonight.

105
00:03:00,850 --> 00:03:01,620
Huh?

106
00:03:01,640 --> 00:03:03,310
I have an acting class
with someone in your dorm.

107
00:03:03,680 --> 00:03:04,100
Who?

108
00:03:04,290 --> 00:03:04,920
Not telling you.

109
00:03:05,550 --> 00:03:07,580
Help! Help! A thief!

110
00:03:07,600 --> 00:03:08,360
- Hey.
- Hey.

111
00:03:08,430 --> 00:03:09,430
Isn't that Dolly?

112
00:03:09,520 --> 00:03:10,750
Yes. Dollar, go!

113
00:03:10,830 --> 00:03:11,490
Dolly!

114
00:03:11,510 --> 00:03:12,120
Dolly!

115
00:03:13,500 --> 00:03:16,810
♫The D Dorm, meet me at the D Dorm♫

116
00:03:17,140 --> 00:03:20,840
♫The D Dorm, meet me at the D Dorm♫

117
00:03:23,310 --> 00:03:28,810
♫Every step we take has a meaning♫

118
00:03:30,590 --> 00:03:35,290
♫No path is ever meaningless♫

119
00:03:37,710 --> 00:03:43,850
♫As long as our hearts keep searching♫

120
00:03:44,820 --> 00:03:49,390
♫One day, we'll find
what we're yearning for♫

121
00:03:49,410 --> 00:03:52,920
♫Walking alone is fine,
but it's better when you're by my side♫

122
00:03:52,940 --> 00:03:56,520
♫It won't be lonely
when you're here to walk beside♫

123
00:03:56,540 --> 00:04:00,060
♫Like a love that waits, waits at the D Dorm♫

124
00:04:00,080 --> 00:04:02,720
♫Like a love that remains,
remains at the dorm♫

125
00:04:02,740 --> 00:04:09,060
♫Meaningful love and good things
await on every path♫

126
00:04:09,500 --> 00:04:16,170
♫It might not be a coincidence
that we get to meet♫

127
00:04:16,649 --> 00:04:23,800
♫There might be hidden meanings
on the path beneath our feet♫

128
00:04:23,820 --> 00:04:30,740
♫Perhaps the D Dorm
is what led me to meet you♫

129
00:04:30,760 --> 00:04:34,880
[The D Dorm]

130
00:04:35,200 --> 00:04:36,290
Dolly, are you alright?

131
00:04:36,320 --> 00:04:36,990
Dolly?

132
00:04:37,010 --> 00:04:38,810
- Are you hurt?
- I'm fine, I'm fine.

133
00:04:38,830 --> 00:04:39,590
Go!

134
00:04:39,610 --> 00:04:41,300
- Oh, no, no, no.
- Whoa, whoa.

135
00:04:50,960 --> 00:04:54,080
[Dome, occupation: police officer/drag queen]

136
00:04:54,100 --> 00:04:55,330
Oh, Teach!

137
00:04:55,659 --> 00:04:56,230
Huh?!

138
00:04:56,980 --> 00:04:57,890
They're my

139
00:04:57,920 --> 00:04:59,420
acting teacher.

140
00:04:59,440 --> 00:05:00,170
Huh?!

141
00:05:00,300 --> 00:05:02,670
By the way, you're so cool, Teach.

142
00:05:02,690 --> 00:05:03,770
Catching a thief like that.

143
00:05:06,140 --> 00:05:07,180
See?

144
00:05:07,310 --> 00:05:08,310
We're lucky

145
00:05:08,340 --> 00:05:09,490
Lieutenant Dome was there.

146
00:05:09,510 --> 00:05:10,230
Huh?!

147
00:05:10,250 --> 00:05:11,930
Dollar, who are you
calling Lieutenant Dome?

148
00:05:11,990 --> 00:05:13,160
I'm off duty,

149
00:05:13,180 --> 00:05:14,960
so call me Queen Dominiga.

150
00:05:14,980 --> 00:05:15,840
Huh?!

151
00:05:15,860 --> 00:05:17,110
What is up with you?

152
00:05:17,130 --> 00:05:18,760
You kept saying, "Huh?!"

153
00:05:19,240 --> 00:05:21,090
I can't process this anymore.

154
00:05:21,220 --> 00:05:22,670
Everything is so confusing.

155
00:05:23,230 --> 00:05:24,590
Either way, thank you very much.

156
00:05:24,710 --> 00:05:26,550
If it weren't for you,
I'd be in real trouble.

157
00:05:26,570 --> 00:05:27,420
Hey,

158
00:05:27,520 --> 00:05:29,020
go heavier today.

159
00:05:29,040 --> 00:05:29,480
Look.

160
00:05:29,580 --> 00:05:32,000
- All muscle, no strength to defend yourself!
- Ow!

161
00:05:32,020 --> 00:05:33,140
Go heavier, got it?!

162
00:05:33,159 --> 00:05:34,460
I have muscles,

163
00:05:34,480 --> 00:05:35,970
but the thief had a knife!

164
00:05:36,100 --> 00:05:37,260
How's that my fault?

165
00:05:38,330 --> 00:05:40,510
He got robbed right outside our dorm.

166
00:05:41,280 --> 00:05:42,280
I don't care.

167
00:05:42,570 --> 00:05:44,200
The dorm has to take responsibility.

168
00:05:45,040 --> 00:05:47,030
So, are you gonna
compensate my son or what?!

169
00:05:47,850 --> 00:05:48,920
If you're not gonna pay,

170
00:05:49,030 --> 00:05:50,730
then lower

171
00:05:50,750 --> 00:05:51,810
my rent.

172
00:05:52,070 --> 00:05:54,500
Whoa, Auntie Duang.

173
00:05:54,520 --> 00:05:57,190
I'm truly sorry. We really
don't have enough security guards.

174
00:05:57,210 --> 00:05:59,620
We'll hire more security guards,

175
00:05:59,640 --> 00:06:02,820
but we'll have to raise
the rent too, Auntie Duang.

176
00:06:05,750 --> 00:06:06,560
Hey,

177
00:06:06,580 --> 00:06:07,990
why would you do that?

178
00:06:08,010 --> 00:06:09,690
Keeping our dorm safe

179
00:06:09,710 --> 00:06:11,500
takes all of us working together.

180
00:06:11,520 --> 00:06:13,310
No need to hire more
security guards. It's a waste!

181
00:06:15,510 --> 00:06:16,840
Oh, that's a relief.

182
00:06:16,860 --> 00:06:18,780
You're taking your brother
to file a police report, right?

183
00:06:18,810 --> 00:06:20,550
Take him too, then.

184
00:06:20,900 --> 00:06:21,560
Mm.

185
00:06:21,990 --> 00:06:23,760
Lieutenant Dome is clocking out.

186
00:06:23,820 --> 00:06:25,110
Now it's time for...

187
00:06:25,130 --> 00:06:26,790
"Queen Dominiga" to entertain you!

188
00:06:27,990 --> 00:06:28,990
Are you ready?

189
00:06:29,010 --> 00:06:30,340
I'm so ready, Mama!

190
00:06:30,360 --> 00:06:31,530
Let's go, Daisy.

191
00:06:31,550 --> 00:06:32,300
Follow me!

192
00:06:32,490 --> 00:06:33,490
Hurry up.

193
00:06:33,510 --> 00:06:34,650
- Let's go. How fabulous.
- Let's go.

194
00:06:34,670 --> 00:06:35,810
You're so annoying.

195
00:06:36,680 --> 00:06:38,670
So? What do you think?

196
00:06:38,690 --> 00:06:41,110
The kids in my dorm

197
00:06:41,310 --> 00:06:43,670
are fabulous, are they not?

198
00:06:45,890 --> 00:06:46,850
Whoa.

199
00:06:46,870 --> 00:06:48,320
That's so deep...deep...deep...

200
00:06:48,400 --> 00:06:49,480
Hello...lo...lo...

201
00:06:49,490 --> 00:06:50,650
Whoa, so deep.

202
00:06:50,909 --> 00:06:52,080
Hey, it's so deep.

203
00:06:52,100 --> 00:06:54,200
If you accidentally fall,
no one would know.

204
00:06:54,370 --> 00:06:55,930
♫I-I-I-I'm not scared♫

205
00:06:55,950 --> 00:06:56,490
Hey!

206
00:06:56,510 --> 00:06:57,470
Hurry up.

207
00:06:57,480 --> 00:06:58,640
I'm hungry, and it's hot.

208
00:06:58,659 --> 00:06:59,990
♫Wait a minute, alright, alright?♫

209
00:07:00,010 --> 00:07:00,590
Hey!

210
00:07:00,610 --> 00:07:01,910
Just say it. No need to sing.

211
00:07:01,990 --> 00:07:03,050
♫I don't know how to say it♫

212
00:07:03,060 --> 00:07:04,090
- ♫How to say it♫
- But I know how to kick you.

213
00:07:06,570 --> 00:07:07,210
Dawin!

214
00:07:07,230 --> 00:07:08,740
Couldn't you catch me with your hands?!

215
00:07:08,760 --> 00:07:09,720
My hands?

216
00:07:09,740 --> 00:07:10,200
Look!

217
00:07:12,070 --> 00:07:13,150
Whoa, that's so red.

218
00:07:13,170 --> 00:07:14,900
You were cheering for a football team, huh?

219
00:07:14,920 --> 00:07:16,300
Are you cheering for
the Red Devils or the Reds?

220
00:07:16,320 --> 00:07:17,530
The Red Brat!

221
00:07:17,930 --> 00:07:19,900
I told Daeng
to fix my water heater yesterday.

222
00:07:20,010 --> 00:07:20,870
You call this fixed?

223
00:07:20,890 --> 00:07:22,350
Hot water came out of the sink

224
00:07:22,380 --> 00:07:23,340
and burned my hands like this!

225
00:07:23,490 --> 00:07:24,830
You told me to fix it,

226
00:07:24,850 --> 00:07:25,750
but you never said

227
00:07:25,770 --> 00:07:27,500
which hole the water should come out of.

228
00:07:27,650 --> 00:07:28,450
What? Hey...

229
00:07:28,470 --> 00:07:29,870
You did this on purpose.

230
00:07:30,190 --> 00:07:31,100
Now my hands are like this.

231
00:07:31,120 --> 00:07:32,300
How am I supposed to work?

232
00:07:32,409 --> 00:07:33,470
That's a good thing, isn't it?

233
00:07:34,070 --> 00:07:35,370
Now you won't be able to trick anyone else

234
00:07:35,390 --> 00:07:36,790
with your fortune-telling!

235
00:07:36,890 --> 00:07:37,690
Fine!

236
00:07:38,290 --> 00:07:39,860
Get ready to lose your job,

237
00:07:39,890 --> 00:07:40,990
unhandyman.

238
00:07:41,190 --> 00:07:42,130
Just wait until

239
00:07:42,150 --> 00:07:44,580
Danis hears about this.
I wonder what she'll say.

240
00:07:46,730 --> 00:07:47,260
Mr. Dawin,

241
00:07:47,270 --> 00:07:48,190
please calm down!

242
00:07:48,210 --> 00:07:49,230
Mr. Dawin!

243
00:07:49,250 --> 00:07:50,400
Hurry up and apologize to him.

244
00:07:50,420 --> 00:07:51,060
What are you waiting for?!

245
00:07:51,080 --> 00:07:52,870
♫I'm still free, you know?♫

246
00:07:52,890 --> 00:07:53,950
Hey! Come here.

247
00:07:53,960 --> 00:07:54,760
Go apologize to him!

248
00:08:09,620 --> 00:08:10,900
Whoa!

249
00:08:10,920 --> 00:08:12,000
Fabulous, Mama!

250
00:08:12,230 --> 00:08:14,020
Come help me first. My back hurts.

251
00:08:14,040 --> 00:08:15,610
Don't just sit there
saying "fabulous." Come on.

252
00:08:15,640 --> 00:08:16,350
Okay, sit down first.

253
00:08:16,360 --> 00:08:17,590
Ow, ow, ow, my back...

254
00:08:17,600 --> 00:08:18,670
- Thank you, dear.
- Are you alright?

255
00:08:18,740 --> 00:08:19,420
Dobby,

256
00:08:19,440 --> 00:08:20,340
you're here anyway.

257
00:08:20,360 --> 00:08:21,990
Ask them

258
00:08:22,010 --> 00:08:23,340
if they know Gaysorn.

259
00:08:25,390 --> 00:08:26,480
Um... Dome?

260
00:08:27,130 --> 00:08:29,730
Call me "Queen Dominiga."

261
00:08:30,930 --> 00:08:32,980
- Queen Dominiga...
- That's right.

262
00:08:33,000 --> 00:08:33,860
- Yes.
- Fabulous.

263
00:08:33,880 --> 00:08:34,669
I want to know

264
00:08:34,690 --> 00:08:36,390
if you have a relative named Gaysorn.

265
00:08:36,409 --> 00:08:38,190
My grandpa is looking for his friend.

266
00:08:38,409 --> 00:08:39,760
A relative named Gaysorn...

267
00:08:39,990 --> 00:08:41,159
I don't have a relative with that name.

268
00:08:41,260 --> 00:08:42,510
But if it's a friend, I do have one.

269
00:08:44,090 --> 00:08:44,920
Look, there!

270
00:08:45,310 --> 00:08:46,950
"Queen Tiger Pollen."

271
00:08:47,280 --> 00:08:47,790
See?

272
00:08:47,810 --> 00:08:50,150
It means "Gaysorn (pollen) of a tiger lily."

273
00:08:52,430 --> 00:08:53,430
