770
00:24:13,610 --> 00:24:14,910
Well, it isn't my office.

771
00:24:14,920 --> 00:24:16,300
But won't it stink up my restaurant?

772
00:24:16,320 --> 00:24:17,860
It won't smell in my office.

773
00:24:17,880 --> 00:24:19,060
We can't hear you at all.

774
00:24:19,680 --> 00:24:20,210
Oh, oops.

775
00:24:20,220 --> 00:24:21,010
Oh...

776
00:24:25,520 --> 00:24:27,600
Dobby,

777
00:24:27,630 --> 00:24:31,780
why do you need to
get into their business?

778
00:24:31,800 --> 00:24:33,470
I do not understand.

779
00:24:33,490 --> 00:24:36,580
Just let Dome feel guilty

780
00:24:36,600 --> 00:24:38,680
for not listening to his brother.

781
00:24:38,700 --> 00:24:39,820
Wait, Grandpa.

782
00:24:39,840 --> 00:24:40,870
Dome didn't do anything wrong.

783
00:24:41,100 --> 00:24:41,990
It's his life.

784
00:24:42,010 --> 00:24:43,610
He gets to choose how to live it.

785
00:24:43,630 --> 00:24:46,210
Being an older brother
doesn't mean you can control his life.

786
00:24:46,230 --> 00:24:47,420
Nonsense!

787
00:24:48,090 --> 00:24:49,770
This is not "control."

788
00:24:49,790 --> 00:24:51,310
He just "means well."

789
00:24:53,520 --> 00:24:54,710
Who turned off the lights?!

790
00:24:54,730 --> 00:24:55,840
Who turned off the lights?!

791
00:24:56,400 --> 00:24:57,210
What...?

792
00:24:57,230 --> 00:24:57,870
Oh...

793
00:24:57,900 --> 00:25:00,490
Is this the pair of glasses
you burned for me?

794
00:25:00,510 --> 00:25:01,830
Don't try to change the topic.

795
00:25:01,840 --> 00:25:04,280
Was pushing my parents out of your house

796
00:25:04,440 --> 00:25:05,880
your way of showing that you meant well?

797
00:25:05,900 --> 00:25:06,800
Yes!

798
00:25:07,130 --> 00:25:08,830
Your mom is stubborn!

799
00:25:08,850 --> 00:25:10,680
And look at her life now.

800
00:25:10,700 --> 00:25:12,150
She is drowning in debts!

801
00:25:12,170 --> 00:25:13,960
Owning a lousy restaurant.

802
00:25:13,980 --> 00:25:16,220
If she would just listen to me...

803
00:25:16,550 --> 00:25:18,600
she wouldn't end up pregnant
by your dad!

804
00:25:20,330 --> 00:25:22,640
If she married the man I found for her,

805
00:25:22,660 --> 00:25:24,450
she would have prospered by now!

806
00:25:26,490 --> 00:25:27,690
Grandpa, when you say that,

807
00:25:28,910 --> 00:25:31,210
does it mean that I was born

808
00:25:32,030 --> 00:25:33,880
to hold Mom back from her fortune?

809
00:25:38,580 --> 00:25:40,490
Dobby, Dobby...

810
00:25:40,780 --> 00:25:42,300
Hey, I...

811
00:25:42,320 --> 00:25:43,530
I did not mean it like that.

812
00:25:43,540 --> 00:25:44,660
Calm down.

813
00:25:44,670 --> 00:25:45,350
What does it mean, then?

814
00:25:45,360 --> 00:25:45,980
Oh, f*ck!

815
00:25:45,990 --> 00:25:47,060
Did you insult me?!

816
00:25:49,470 --> 00:25:50,490
I'm not insulting you.

817
00:25:50,510 --> 00:25:51,270
I'm insulting your outfit.

818
00:25:54,240 --> 00:25:55,550
How the hell did it get here?

819
00:25:56,480 --> 00:25:57,400
- Whoa!
- Whoa!

820
00:25:59,190 --> 00:26:00,630
Hey, Dobby!

821
00:26:00,730 --> 00:26:01,630
You...

822
00:26:01,790 --> 00:26:03,480
You have to burn a new outfit for me.

823
00:26:03,500 --> 00:26:05,120
I cannot go around looking like this.

824
00:26:05,150 --> 00:26:06,830
It's embarrassing!

825
00:26:06,980 --> 00:26:08,090
Why would you be embarrassed?

826
00:26:08,110 --> 00:26:09,190
I'm the only person who can see you.

827
00:26:09,210 --> 00:26:10,570
And you won't be embarrassed anymore,

828
00:26:10,590 --> 00:26:11,450
because I'm leaving.

829
00:26:11,460 --> 00:26:12,460
I'm going home!

830
00:26:12,990 --> 00:26:15,140
What about finding Gaysorn?

831
00:26:17,480 --> 00:26:18,550
The search for Grandma Gaysorn?

832
00:26:18,570 --> 00:26:19,310
Mm...

833
00:26:19,380 --> 00:26:21,110
Go ask the others for help, Grandpa.

834
00:26:21,130 --> 00:26:22,840
Because a burden like me,

835
00:26:22,860 --> 00:26:24,500
won't be able to help you.

836
00:26:25,310 --> 00:26:26,480
You are a grown man,

837
00:26:26,500 --> 00:26:27,950
but you still hold a grudge?!

838
00:26:28,120 --> 00:26:30,390
The burden I was talking about

839
00:26:30,410 --> 00:26:32,680
was your father!

840
00:26:32,700 --> 00:26:35,260
You assumed things on your own!

841
00:26:35,280 --> 00:26:36,320
Oh, wow...

842
00:26:36,720 --> 00:26:38,340
I went all in.

843
00:26:38,790 --> 00:26:40,010
Do you ever think that

844
00:26:40,030 --> 00:26:41,980
the reason Mom and Dad left

845
00:26:41,990 --> 00:26:43,910
was because you were
stopping them from being happy?

846
00:26:46,100 --> 00:26:48,300
What would you know?!

847
00:26:48,320 --> 00:26:50,310
The reason I worked so hard

848
00:26:50,330 --> 00:26:53,150
to build this dorm,

849
00:26:53,170 --> 00:26:54,590
it was all for your mother,

850
00:26:54,610 --> 00:26:56,350
so she would be able to live comfortably!

851
00:26:56,370 --> 00:26:58,300
If she was truly happy,

852
00:26:58,490 --> 00:26:59,470
why did she run away?

853
00:27:01,800 --> 00:27:03,640
Well, your mother is stubborn!

854
00:27:04,020 --> 00:27:06,410
She did not want to live

855
00:27:06,430 --> 00:27:07,450
comfortably!

856
00:27:07,470 --> 00:27:10,680
Instead, she ran away to a hard life
with your father in Nakhon Sawan!

857
00:27:11,400 --> 00:27:12,640
You wouldn't understand.

858
00:27:12,760 --> 00:27:14,150
Have you ever gone to check in on Mom

859
00:27:14,260 --> 00:27:15,880
after she ran away?!

860
00:27:15,890 --> 00:27:16,940
How could you know...?

861
00:27:19,000 --> 00:27:19,920
Ugh! Whatever.

862
00:27:19,940 --> 00:27:21,690
I'm going to sell this dorm.

863
00:27:21,710 --> 00:27:23,640
Mom and I don't want to keep it!

864
00:27:24,010 --> 00:27:25,010
Go ahead!

865
00:27:25,240 --> 00:27:26,630
If this dorm

866
00:27:27,090 --> 00:27:29,370
is such an eyesore for you,

867
00:27:29,400 --> 00:27:31,350
then sell it!

868
00:27:31,640 --> 00:27:32,550
And you...

869
00:27:32,820 --> 00:27:33,650
get out!

870
00:27:33,660 --> 00:27:35,150
Get out of here! Go!

871
00:27:35,170 --> 00:27:36,280
Yeah, I'll leave, alright!

872
00:27:36,370 --> 00:27:37,090
Go!

873
00:27:39,890 --> 00:27:42,380
Like mother, like son!

874
00:27:42,400 --> 00:27:45,600
How frustrating!

875
00:27:50,790 --> 00:27:52,570
Hello, Mom, I'm coming home today.

876
00:27:54,800 --> 00:27:55,600
Oh...

877
00:27:55,620 --> 00:27:57,880
I'm a bit sick of seeing
some people at the dorm.

878
00:27:58,590 --> 00:28:00,990
To be honest, I miss your cooking too.

879
00:28:03,590 --> 00:28:05,900
I don't think there will be traffic.
It'll probably take two hours.

880
00:28:08,590 --> 00:28:09,390
Mom,

881
00:28:09,780 --> 00:28:10,990
can I ask you something?

882
00:28:11,990 --> 00:28:13,630
Have you ever regretted

883
00:28:13,650 --> 00:28:15,020
running away to be with Dad?

884
00:28:16,710 --> 00:28:17,310
Huh?!

885
00:28:18,370 --> 00:28:20,110
You regret not taking
Grandpa's money with you?

886
00:28:20,560 --> 00:28:21,230
Huh?

887
00:28:21,240 --> 00:28:22,580
Are you a scammer or something?

888
00:28:23,050 --> 00:28:24,690
Well...you're funny, Mom.

889
00:28:25,360 --> 00:28:26,600
Yeah, I'm on my way.

890
00:28:26,870 --> 00:28:27,780
Miss you.

891
00:28:27,790 --> 00:28:28,870
Muah, muah!

892
00:28:32,910 --> 00:28:33,910
Oh...

893
00:28:34,990 --> 00:28:35,990
Hey...

894
00:28:37,380 --> 00:28:38,380
Dollar,

895
00:28:38,550 --> 00:28:39,300
how did it go?

896
00:28:39,320 --> 00:28:40,560
Did you catch up with Din?

897
00:28:40,700 --> 00:28:42,240
Did you speak for Dome?

898
00:28:43,510 --> 00:28:44,510
Why are you crying?

899
00:28:44,530 --> 00:28:45,700
Did you fight?

900
00:28:45,720 --> 00:28:47,170
I pulled my eyelashes and it hurts.

901
00:28:47,190 --> 00:28:49,160
- Oh...
- Oh...

902
00:28:50,190 --> 00:28:50,810
And...

903
00:28:50,820 --> 00:28:52,840
I don't know where Din went.
We haven't talked.

904
00:28:53,090 --> 00:28:54,190
You don't have to talk to him.

905
00:28:54,910 --> 00:28:55,910
It won't change anything.

906
00:28:55,930 --> 00:28:57,160
In his eyes,

907
00:28:57,180 --> 00:28:58,530
I never grew up.

908
00:29:00,720 --> 00:29:02,200
I'm just a little brother...

909
00:29:02,690 --> 00:29:03,930
who can't think for myself.

910
00:29:03,950 --> 00:29:05,360
A brother who only causes trouble.

911
00:29:07,900 --> 00:29:08,800
Dominiga,

912
00:29:09,010 --> 00:29:10,330
don't be sad.

913
00:29:10,350 --> 00:29:11,910
No matter what people say,

914
00:29:11,930 --> 00:29:14,590
I'll always be by your side.

915
00:29:15,900 --> 00:29:17,770
Just like what NewJiew said,

916
00:29:18,280 --> 00:29:20,400
"If you don't love me, don't act nice
or act like you care."

917
00:29:20,510 --> 00:29:22,640
"If you don't love me,
don't try to protect or order me around."

918
00:29:22,660 --> 00:29:24,640
- "'Cause my heart is fragile."
- "'Cause my heart is fragile."

919
00:29:25,590 --> 00:29:27,070
- Wow...
- That was perfect.

920
00:29:27,090 --> 00:29:28,380
You did that perfectly, dear.

921
00:29:29,290 --> 00:29:30,250
You were dancing, does it mean

922
00:29:30,260 --> 00:29:32,220
that you're not mad at Din anymore?

923
00:29:33,970 --> 00:29:36,280
I wasn't that mad at Din,

924
00:29:36,670 --> 00:29:38,600
but my family is like this.

925
00:29:38,750 --> 00:29:40,150
They put limitations on me
ever since I was young.

926
00:29:40,170 --> 00:29:41,880
Whether it's what I study or what I do...

927
00:29:42,280 --> 00:29:44,380
They never asked if
I'm fine with those things.

928
00:29:44,390 --> 00:29:46,230
Ugh...

929
00:29:46,250 --> 00:29:47,690
Dollar is like that too!

930
00:29:48,710 --> 00:29:49,740
Back then,

931
00:29:49,760 --> 00:29:52,470
he tried to force me into
the Police Cadet Academy.

932
00:29:53,680 --> 00:29:55,030
But I didn't listen.

933
00:29:55,050 --> 00:29:57,710
When he couldn't force me mentally,

934
00:29:57,740 --> 00:30:00,040
he forced me

935
00:30:00,060 --> 00:30:01,630
to exercise physically instead!

936
00:30:01,670 --> 00:30:03,310
- Look.
- Ooh, mm...

937
00:30:03,580 --> 00:30:04,810
- Ugh...
- It's solid.

938
00:30:04,830 --> 00:30:06,550
I was worried about you back then,

939
00:30:06,570 --> 00:30:08,370
because the fashion major
you wanted to get into

940
00:30:08,390 --> 00:30:10,160
didn't look like it could
provide for you.

941
00:30:10,180 --> 00:30:11,800
You must think about your future, too.

942
00:30:11,820 --> 00:30:13,300
If I wasn't here with you,

943
00:30:13,320 --> 00:30:14,710
how will you and Mom live?

944
00:30:14,720 --> 00:30:16,100
Your words are wise,

945
00:30:16,950 --> 00:30:18,830
but your eyelashes are so extra.

946
00:30:19,950 --> 00:30:21,550
Let me take them off for you.

947
00:30:21,860 --> 00:30:22,790
I'll pull them off.

948
00:30:22,810 --> 00:30:24,830
Leave my eyelashes alone!

949
00:30:24,850 --> 00:30:26,180
Hey...

950
00:30:26,610 --> 00:30:27,870
Hey, Dome,

951
00:30:28,060 --> 00:30:29,060
I think Din

952
00:30:29,470 --> 00:30:30,920
didn't want to cut ties with you.

953
00:30:32,110 --> 00:30:33,110
The reason he did that

954
00:30:33,130 --> 00:30:34,690
was because he was worried.

955
00:30:35,330 --> 00:30:36,550
Just like how I'm

956
00:30:36,570 --> 00:30:37,910
worried about Dolly.

957
00:30:40,610 --> 00:30:42,220
I understand,

958
00:30:42,590 --> 00:30:44,010
but I don't think it's fair

959
00:30:44,600 --> 00:30:45,890
Din got to become a police.

960
00:30:46,130 --> 00:30:47,470
He gets to do what he loves.

961
00:30:48,710 --> 00:30:49,810
What about me?

962
00:30:50,010 --> 00:30:52,000
Can't I do something
I love as well?

963
00:30:58,180 --> 00:30:59,760
Then are you sure

964
00:30:59,780 --> 00:31:02,160
that the job you love

965
00:31:02,190 --> 00:31:03,910
can actually sustain you?

966
00:31:05,150 --> 00:31:06,520
Hey, Dominiga,

967
00:31:06,980 --> 00:31:08,300
tell him.

968
00:31:08,320 --> 00:31:11,370
Say it with confidence.

969
00:31:12,930 --> 00:31:13,560
No.

970
00:31:16,230 --> 00:31:18,230
- I lost my footing...
- I'm just saying that

971
00:31:18,250 --> 00:31:19,840
I'll try my best.

972
00:31:19,990 --> 00:31:21,620
Because in his eyes,

973
00:31:21,640 --> 00:31:23,800
working as a drag queen

974
00:31:23,820 --> 00:31:25,010
is an unstable job.

975
00:31:25,390 --> 00:31:27,190
But wouldn't it be better

976
00:31:27,240 --> 00:31:30,200
if I get to do what I truly enjoy?

977
00:31:33,190 --> 00:31:34,790
Your younger brother said it.

978
00:31:35,690 --> 00:31:36,830
What do you think, big brother?

979
00:31:36,850 --> 00:31:38,000
- Huh?
- Huh?

980
00:31:45,210 --> 00:31:46,600
But what if...

981
00:31:47,260 --> 00:31:49,090
it doesn't work out?

982
00:31:50,000 --> 00:31:51,530
What will you do with your life?

983
00:31:58,090 --> 00:32:00,200
I'll have to find a new job, Din.

984
00:32:00,840 --> 00:32:02,230
But not a police.

985
00:32:05,450 --> 00:32:06,590
To be honest,

986
00:32:07,590 --> 00:32:09,010
there is no job

987
00:32:09,290 --> 00:32:10,510
that's a hundred percent stable.

988
00:32:10,900 --> 00:32:12,030
It depends...

989
00:32:12,330 --> 00:32:14,190
on how you live your life.

990
00:32:15,190 --> 00:32:18,220
Din, please give me a chance.

991
00:32:28,200 --> 00:32:29,740
Then we should head home, have a meal,

992
00:32:31,730 --> 00:32:32,930
and talk to our parents about this.

993
00:32:34,350 --> 00:32:35,680
If they disagree,

994
00:32:36,790 --> 00:32:38,110
I'll try to talk to them.

995
00:32:38,820 --> 00:32:39,860
Really?!

996
00:32:43,230 --> 00:32:45,040
- Let's go, then!
- Hey, wait.

997
00:32:45,060 --> 00:32:46,130
You should get changed,

998
00:32:46,150 --> 00:32:47,800
- or our parents might have a heart attack.
- Get changed?

999
00:32:47,820 --> 00:32:48,700
Okay.

1000
00:32:48,720 --> 00:32:50,590
- Change your outfit.
- Change, change.

1001
00:32:50,650 --> 00:32:51,280
Get changed.

1002
00:32:52,060 --> 00:32:52,900
Thank you, Din,

1003
00:32:52,920 --> 00:32:53,720
for listening to Dome.

1004
00:32:53,740 --> 00:32:54,780
Ugh!

1005
00:32:55,170 --> 00:32:56,070
Can I ask you one thing?

1006
00:32:56,230 --> 00:32:57,230
Will you remove your eyelashes?

1007
00:32:57,670 --> 00:32:58,990
It's annoying to look at.

1008
00:32:59,010 --> 00:32:59,770
You don't like it?

1009
00:32:59,790 --> 00:33:00,690
No, I don't!

1010
00:33:00,710 --> 00:33:01,620
- Stop!
- You don't like it?

1011
00:33:01,640 --> 00:33:02,510
Go take them off.

1012
00:33:03,430 --> 00:33:04,100
But it's pretty.

1013
00:33:04,130 --> 00:33:05,000
Hey, take your friend away.

1014
00:33:05,030 --> 00:33:06,520
Hello, this is Daisy.

1015
00:33:09,420 --> 00:33:10,880
I was...practicing my script earlier.

1016
00:33:10,990 --> 00:33:11,590
Huh?!

1017
00:33:12,400 --> 00:33:13,680
You can't contact Dobby?

1018
00:33:16,000 --> 00:33:17,000
Dobby.

1019
00:33:18,120 --> 00:33:18,800
Dobby.

1020
00:33:19,070 --> 00:33:19,960
Are you here?

1021
00:33:20,600 --> 00:33:23,590
Oh, why am I hiding?
He cannot see me anyway.

1022
00:33:23,680 --> 00:33:24,340
Dobby.

1023
00:33:27,300 --> 00:33:28,180
Dobby!

1024
00:33:32,680 --> 00:33:33,680
His bag isn't here as well.

1025
00:33:34,290 --> 00:33:36,720
How could it be here?
He already went to Nakhon Sawan.

1026
00:33:37,090 --> 00:33:37,990
Dobby...

1027
00:33:39,030 --> 00:33:40,580
But his car is still here.

1028
00:33:43,190 --> 00:33:43,860
Gramps.

1029
00:33:44,390 --> 00:33:45,860
Gramps, Gramps.

1030
00:33:46,010 --> 00:33:47,430
If you can hear me,

1031
00:33:47,610 --> 00:33:48,990
please help me look for Dobby.

1032
00:33:49,240 --> 00:33:50,710
His mother is very worried.

1033
00:33:52,290 --> 00:33:53,870
Please tell him to call his mother back.

1034
00:33:54,000 --> 00:33:54,880
Thank you.

1035
00:33:55,490 --> 00:33:56,490
Thank you, Gramps.

1036
00:33:58,410 --> 00:34:00,210
What does this have to do with me?!

1037
00:34:00,980 --> 00:34:03,890
It is not my duty to look for him!

1038
00:34:09,300 --> 00:34:10,690
Maybe I should look for him...

1039
00:34:11,290 --> 00:34:12,600
So that he...

1040
00:34:13,190 --> 00:34:14,510
burns me a new outfit.

1041
00:34:20,010 --> 00:34:21,280
Dobby!

1042
00:34:21,810 --> 00:34:22,830
Dobby!

1043
00:34:24,010 --> 00:34:24,940
Dobby?

1044
00:34:24,969 --> 00:34:26,909
Dobby, where are you?

1045
00:34:26,929 --> 00:34:28,060
Dobby!

1046
00:34:29,040 --> 00:34:30,440
Dobby!

1047
00:34:30,460 --> 00:34:31,510
Dobby!

1048
00:34:33,199 --> 00:34:37,699
Dobby!

1049
00:34:38,699 --> 00:34:39,920
Dobby!

1050
00:34:39,940 --> 00:34:43,080
Hey, do you still exist?
I can't find you anywhere!

1051
00:34:43,100 --> 00:34:44,100
Dobby!

1052
00:34:45,610 --> 00:34:46,670
Dobby!

1053
00:34:46,690 --> 00:34:49,100
Dobby, where are...

1054
00:34:49,120 --> 00:34:49,679
Oh?

1055
00:34:50,130 --> 00:34:51,310
The manhole cover is open.

1056
00:34:51,330 --> 00:34:53,350
Oh...that's dangerous.

1057
00:34:53,370 --> 00:34:55,760
Someone might fall in there.

1058
00:34:55,780 --> 00:34:57,830
It's probably Daeng the Handyman's fault.

1059
00:34:58,460 --> 00:35:00,950
Oh, this is...

1060
00:35:01,290 --> 00:35:01,840
Huh?!

1061
00:35:04,090 --> 00:35:05,000
Dobby.

1062
00:35:05,090 --> 00:35:06,810
Help, please help Dobby!

1063
00:35:06,830 --> 00:35:08,140
Hold on, alright?

1064
00:35:08,160 --> 00:35:09,720
I will find someone to help you.

1065
00:35:09,740 --> 00:35:10,970
Anybody!

1066
00:35:10,990 --> 00:35:11,760
Help!

1067
00:35:11,790 --> 00:35:13,420
Dobby fell down the sewer!

1068
00:35:13,440 --> 00:35:16,510
Dobby!!

1069
00:35:19,910 --> 00:35:20,920
Ugh...

1070
00:35:26,800 --> 00:35:27,930
why do you have to
keep this up?

1071
00:35:27,950 --> 00:35:30,300
Just say you'll make up and
be friends,

1072
00:35:30,320 --> 00:35:31,870
and we'll let you go to the toilet.

1073
00:35:32,180 --> 00:35:32,940
Yes.

1074
00:35:33,190 --> 00:35:35,370
I don't mind doing that.

1075
00:35:35,590 --> 00:35:36,870
I can make up with him,

1076
00:35:38,300 --> 00:35:39,410
but he has to apologize first!

1077
00:35:39,440 --> 00:35:40,310
Oh...

1078
00:35:40,560 --> 00:35:42,490
Never...

1079
00:35:43,160 --> 00:35:43,950
Oh...

1080
00:35:45,920 --> 00:35:46,920
Ow...

1081
00:35:47,430 --> 00:35:48,800
I think we should let them go.

1082
00:35:48,820 --> 00:35:50,010
If they pee themselves here,

1083
00:35:50,030 --> 00:35:50,690
who will clean it up?

1084
00:35:50,710 --> 00:35:51,370
No.

1085
00:35:51,990 --> 00:35:53,470
They'll have to clean it on their own.

1086
00:35:54,920 --> 00:35:56,370
Think about

1087
00:35:56,390 --> 00:35:57,640
what you're going to do next.

1088
00:35:57,660 --> 00:35:58,660
Since I'm

1089
00:35:58,680 --> 00:35:59,760
not in a rush anyway.

1090
00:36:01,910 --> 00:36:03,100
I'll turn on the music while I wait.

1091
00:36:04,510 --> 00:36:08,520
♫Let it flow out♫

1092
00:36:25,350 --> 00:36:25,970
Everyone!

1093
00:36:25,990 --> 00:36:27,190
- Huh?
- Everyone, everyone!

1094
00:36:27,210 --> 00:36:27,920
Whoa...

1095
00:36:28,190 --> 00:36:29,640
Has anyone seen Mr. Dobby?

1096
00:36:29,660 --> 00:36:30,760
What's wrong, Guard Dum?

1097
00:36:30,890 --> 00:36:32,150
Mr. Dobby went missing.

1098
00:36:32,170 --> 00:36:33,180
- Huh?!
- Huh?!

1099
00:36:33,510 --> 00:36:36,630
Mr. Dax, Mr. Dolly, and Mr. Dollar were
searching. No one could contact him!

1100
00:36:36,650 --> 00:36:38,660
- Everyone, let's go find Dobby!
- Whoa....

1101
00:36:38,680 --> 00:36:40,000
- Ow, ow, ow.
- Guard Dum, go!

1102
00:36:40,020 --> 00:36:41,470
- Lead the way, Guard Dum.
- Where is he?!

1103
00:36:41,490 --> 00:36:42,630
- Quickly!
- Guard Dum, go!

1104
00:36:42,660 --> 00:36:44,840
Don't leave yet. Let me go...

1105
00:36:44,860 --> 00:36:46,120
Ugh, stop shouting.

1106
00:36:46,140 --> 00:36:46,950
The key is right there.

1107
00:36:49,300 --> 00:36:50,910
It's so far away,

1108
00:36:50,930 --> 00:36:51,860
I can't reach it!

1109
00:36:51,910 --> 00:36:53,220
We can, we have to.

1110
00:36:53,740 --> 00:36:54,520
Oh!

1111
00:36:55,130 --> 00:36:56,610
Put your arm here.

1112
00:36:59,910 --> 00:37:00,800
Ow...

1113
00:37:04,300 --> 00:37:04,930
Hey!

1114
00:37:06,560 --> 00:37:07,560
Whoa!

1115
00:37:24,750 --> 00:37:26,610
Duang!
[Duangjai's Kitchen, Made-to-Order Food]

1116
00:37:26,630 --> 00:37:27,300
Danis!

1117
00:37:27,320 --> 00:37:28,580
Where did they all go?

1118
00:37:28,600 --> 00:37:30,830
Come help Dobby!

1119
00:37:30,850 --> 00:37:33,100
How can I help him? I can't!

1120
00:37:40,130 --> 00:37:41,520
- Gramps?!
- Gramps?!

1121
00:37:44,130 --> 00:37:45,040
You can see me?

1122
00:37:46,590 --> 00:37:49,750
Go help Dobby! He fell down the sewer!

1123
00:37:50,670 --> 00:37:54,480
A ghost!

1124
00:38:00,330 --> 00:38:01,580
Was that real?

1125
00:38:02,090 --> 00:38:03,090
What the heck?!

1126
00:38:03,600 --> 00:38:04,600
Gramps!

1127
00:38:05,000 --> 00:38:10,320
[The D Dorm]

1128
00:38:11,890 --> 00:38:12,890
Here's your medicine.

1129
00:38:14,430 --> 00:38:15,850
- Ow...
- Thanks a lot.

1130
00:38:15,880 --> 00:38:16,880
Whoa.

1131
00:38:18,510 --> 00:38:20,170
- It stings...
- Are you really alright?

1132
00:38:23,100 --> 00:38:23,600
Whoa.

1133
00:38:24,010 --> 00:38:25,670
You got a head injury.

1134
00:38:25,690 --> 00:38:26,710
Is your brain still working?

1135
00:38:26,850 --> 00:38:27,910
Do you remember who I am?

1136
00:38:30,670 --> 00:38:31,990
Would you like me to call you
Dax or Daisy, then?

1137
00:38:32,010 --> 00:38:32,780
Oh,

1138
00:38:32,800 --> 00:38:34,290
you can call me Daisy.

1139
00:38:34,310 --> 00:38:36,840
- Come here, let me give you a smooch.
- Hey!

1140
00:38:36,860 --> 00:38:37,860
Dax, stop!

1141
00:38:37,890 --> 00:38:39,490
Don't, don't, don't, Dax!

1142
00:38:40,440 --> 00:38:41,550
- Dax, don't tease me! Ow!
- Whoa!

1143
00:38:41,790 --> 00:38:43,150
- Dax, stop. It hurts!
- Whoa!

1144
00:38:43,170 --> 00:38:46,420
Am I interrupting something?
I can come back later.

1145
00:38:46,440 --> 00:38:47,280
Hey!

1146
00:38:47,300 --> 00:38:48,140
Hey, hey, hey, wait!

1147
00:38:48,160 --> 00:38:49,630
- Get off me, Dax!
- What?

1148
00:38:49,650 --> 00:38:50,950
- What is it?
- Don't play along.

1149
00:38:50,980 --> 00:38:51,640
Oh, okay.

1150
00:38:51,660 --> 00:38:52,590
What do you need?

1151
00:38:52,610 --> 00:38:54,480
I brought you a first-aid kit.

1152
00:38:54,500 --> 00:38:56,960
So after you take a shower,
you can change your bandage.

1153
00:38:56,980 --> 00:38:58,110
Oh, you may continue.

1154
00:38:58,130 --> 00:38:59,900
- Huh? Don't go yet.
- Wait, wait.

1155
00:38:59,920 --> 00:39:01,200
By the way,

1156
00:39:01,220 --> 00:39:03,190
I told Daeng the Handyman to
close the manhole cover.

1157
00:39:03,610 --> 00:39:05,800
Don't be mad at him, alright?

1158
00:39:05,820 --> 00:39:07,880
He didn't mean to be careless.

1159
00:39:07,900 --> 00:39:08,900
Just...

1160
00:39:09,390 --> 00:39:10,790
Some stuff happened...

1161
00:39:11,100 --> 00:39:13,040
Thank you for saving me.

1162
00:39:13,890 --> 00:39:15,240
No need to thank me.

1163
00:39:15,260 --> 00:39:16,260
You should thank Gramps.

1164
00:39:16,560 --> 00:39:17,990
- Huh?
- Mm.

1165
00:39:20,120 --> 00:39:21,590
Dawin told me

1166
00:39:21,610 --> 00:39:23,720
Gramps suddenly showed up

1167
00:39:23,740 --> 00:39:25,090
to tell him that you...

1168
00:39:25,110 --> 00:39:26,950
fell down the sewer. And sent him to help you.

1169
00:39:26,970 --> 00:39:27,670
Huh?!

1170
00:39:27,690 --> 00:39:28,900
Dawin saw Grandpa?

1171
00:39:28,930 --> 00:39:29,930
That's what he told me.

1172
00:39:29,950 --> 00:39:31,140
Don't believe him too much.

1173
00:39:31,340 --> 00:39:33,490
He was probably delirious
from holding in his pee.

1174
00:39:33,510 --> 00:39:34,320
- I see...
- Well...

1175
00:39:34,420 --> 00:39:35,810
What did he say again?

1176
00:39:35,830 --> 00:39:38,510
Gramps was wearing drag
then he...hey!

1177
00:39:38,530 --> 00:39:39,410
- Dobby!
- You...

1178
00:39:39,430 --> 00:39:39,940
What's wrong, Dobby?

1179
00:39:39,970 --> 00:39:41,220
Hey, are you alright?

1180
00:39:41,240 --> 00:39:42,990
- Dobby, did you choke?
- I'm fine.

1181
00:39:43,010 --> 00:39:43,870
- I'm fine, Ms. Danis.
- Dobby...

1182
00:39:43,900 --> 00:39:45,070
But I'm not fine because of you.

1183
00:39:45,090 --> 00:39:45,680
What?

1184
00:39:45,700 --> 00:39:47,460
- Was it too soft?
- Oh, it's too harsh.

1185
00:39:47,960 --> 00:39:49,310
- Hit me gently. It hurts.
- Ugh.

1186
00:39:49,330 --> 00:39:51,970
Take care of yourself, then.
I'm tired of you guys.

1187
00:39:52,690 --> 00:39:53,270
Hey.

1188
00:39:53,480 --> 00:39:55,590
Stop hitting me and go
look for something to help me.

1189
00:39:55,620 --> 00:39:56,690
Aw, aren't we going to continue?

1190
00:39:56,710 --> 00:39:58,180
That's enough!

1191
00:39:58,200 --> 00:39:59,470
Here, I'll dress your wound.

1192
00:40:02,880 --> 00:40:03,950
We don't have any Mia cloth.

1193
00:40:04,220 --> 00:40:04,970
What? Mia cloth?

1194
00:40:04,990 --> 00:40:05,630
Goth.

1195
00:40:05,660 --> 00:40:06,660
Wow...

1196
00:40:07,000 --> 00:40:07,740
Ow...

1197
00:40:07,760 --> 00:40:08,270
- It hurts even worse.
- Oh...

1198
00:40:08,290 --> 00:40:09,510
Did you laugh to the point that it hurt?

1199
00:40:09,530 --> 00:40:10,530
It's your joke that hurts.

1200
00:40:11,180 --> 00:40:12,120
- Let me look around.
- Quickly.

1201
00:40:12,140 --> 00:40:13,910
Just find one.

1202
00:40:19,780 --> 00:40:20,780
Whoa...

1203
00:40:22,290 --> 00:40:23,700
It's a big wound, too.

1204
00:40:24,580 --> 00:40:25,890
Is this your house?

1205
00:40:27,000 --> 00:40:27,850
Here.

1206
00:40:31,440 --> 00:40:33,720
- Whoa.
- Is this kid you?

1207
00:41:11,700 --> 00:41:13,800
Dobby, are you hurt?

1208
00:41:14,330 --> 00:41:15,110
I am hurt.

1209
00:41:15,410 --> 00:41:16,080
Huh?

1210
00:41:16,300 --> 00:41:17,530
I fell down a sewer, you know?

1211
00:41:18,290 --> 00:41:19,450
You were not asleep?

1212
00:41:22,080 --> 00:41:23,510
I couldn't fall asleep, Grandpa.

1213
00:41:25,200 --> 00:41:26,540
I want to ask you something.

1214
00:41:26,810 --> 00:41:27,810
What?

1215
00:41:28,990 --> 00:41:31,190
Ever since Mom went to live with Dad,

1216
00:41:31,600 --> 00:41:33,360
have you ever gone to
check in on her?

1217
00:41:47,440 --> 00:41:49,180
Why did you go find her, Grandpa?

1218
00:41:49,790 --> 00:41:51,640
Didn't you already cut ties with her?

1219
00:41:56,050 --> 00:41:57,310
I just wanted to see

1220
00:41:57,330 --> 00:42:01,520
the state of her
after she left to be with your father.

1221
00:42:04,400 --> 00:42:05,710
You missed my mom, didn't you?

1222
00:42:13,810 --> 00:42:16,180
That is none of your business.

1223
00:42:16,200 --> 00:42:17,350
What about you?

1224
00:42:17,370 --> 00:42:19,090
You said you would go back to
Nakhon Sawan

1225
00:42:19,110 --> 00:42:21,950
to that little rat hole house
of yours, did you not?

1226
00:42:22,820 --> 00:42:24,020
How can I go back, Grandpa?

1227
00:42:24,040 --> 00:42:25,600
Look at me.

1228
00:42:25,620 --> 00:42:26,580
Look.

1229
00:42:26,600 --> 00:42:27,600
Look!

1230
00:42:28,500 --> 00:42:31,000
If I went back looking like this,

1231
00:42:31,550 --> 00:42:32,550
your dorm

1232
00:42:32,680 --> 00:42:34,560
would be destroyed.

1233
00:42:35,450 --> 00:42:36,180
Oh...

1234
00:42:36,470 --> 00:42:39,390
Take some rest, then.

1235
00:42:40,880 --> 00:42:42,790
I do not want you to perish.

1236
00:42:42,820 --> 00:42:44,770
Because if you did,

1237
00:42:44,790 --> 00:42:48,240
there will be two ghosts in the same den.

1238
00:42:51,090 --> 00:42:53,110
You do not have to thank me.

1239
00:42:53,130 --> 00:42:54,680
Just...

1240
00:42:54,700 --> 00:42:56,510
burn me a new outfit.

1241
00:42:56,530 --> 00:42:57,920
That would be enough.

1242
00:42:57,940 --> 00:43:00,430
Because each time I look at this outfit,

1243
00:43:00,450 --> 00:43:03,000
it reminds me of a movie.
I cannot recall the name...

1244
00:43:03,020 --> 00:43:06,200
The director is called Poj Arnon.

1245
00:43:06,220 --> 00:43:07,600
He made a lot of movies.

1246
00:43:07,620 --> 00:43:09,060
There is this one scene

1247
00:43:09,080 --> 00:43:11,590
in which a character said,

1248
00:43:11,610 --> 00:43:13,150
"Who killed Araya"?

1249
00:43:13,170 --> 00:43:14,310
And another person answered,

1250
00:43:14,600 --> 00:43:15,710
"Payoon..."

1251
00:43:15,890 --> 00:43:16,930
Then she went quiet.

1252
00:43:16,960 --> 00:43:18,100
And suddenly, she said,

1253
00:43:18,210 --> 00:43:19,110
"is not the killer!"

1254
00:43:19,130 --> 00:43:20,410
So the other person replied,

1255
00:43:20,640 --> 00:43:22,390
"You timed that so horribly"!

1256
00:43:23,110 --> 00:43:24,500
Oh, it made me laugh.

1257
00:43:24,530 --> 00:43:25,560
I really liked that one.

1258
00:43:25,580 --> 00:43:27,600
- Ow, ow...
- It is stuck in my head.

1259
00:43:28,360 --> 00:43:29,190
- You...
- Go watch it.

1260
00:43:29,210 --> 00:43:30,070
You don't remember the name,

1261
00:43:30,090 --> 00:43:31,130
- but you remember all the dialogues?
- Yeah.

1262
00:43:31,150 --> 00:43:32,550
But I really enjoyed it.

1263
00:43:32,570 --> 00:43:33,130
- You did?
- Yeah.

1264
00:43:33,150 --> 00:43:34,510
- Yeah.
- I'll go watch it.

1265
00:43:34,540 --> 00:43:35,430
I liked it.

1266
00:43:35,450 --> 00:43:37,380
Go argue with
yourself outside, Grandpa.

1267
00:43:37,410 --> 00:43:38,950
Oh, rest up.

1268
00:43:38,980 --> 00:43:40,680
But you have to watch it.

1269
00:43:40,700 --> 00:43:42,010
- Yeah, I got it.
- Good.

1270
00:43:44,200 --> 00:43:49,500
♫It might not be a coincidence
that we get to meet♫

1271
00:43:50,840 --> 00:43:51,640
Call out to him.

1272
00:43:51,660 --> 00:43:53,060
Hey!

1273
00:43:54,160 --> 00:43:54,690
Ugh.

1274
00:43:54,710 --> 00:43:56,050
Stop making loud noises.

1275
00:43:56,070 --> 00:43:57,760
It's disturbing other tenants!

1276
00:43:58,390 --> 00:44:00,330
Who told you about us?

1277
00:44:00,440 --> 00:44:01,440
I did.

1278
00:44:01,630 --> 00:44:02,490
Kappa?

1279
00:44:02,880 --> 00:44:04,450
- Would you like this, then?!
- Whoa, whoa, whoa.

1280
00:44:04,470 --> 00:44:05,880
Whoa, whoa, whoa.

1281
00:44:05,900 --> 00:44:06,760
Dawin!

1282
00:44:06,780 --> 00:44:08,380
Why do you want to see
Gramps' ghost again?

1283
00:44:08,400 --> 00:44:10,660
I just want to prove

1284
00:44:10,700 --> 00:44:12,180
if I have the ability to see ghosts.

1285
00:44:12,200 --> 00:44:13,210
I tried it all.

1286
00:44:13,230 --> 00:44:14,620
From looking between my legs

1287
00:44:14,640 --> 00:44:16,290
to wearing dead people's clothes.

1288
00:44:16,310 --> 00:44:17,950
But there's one method I haven't tried yet.

1289
00:44:18,230 --> 00:44:19,310
Would you like to try it out tonight?

1290
00:44:22,840 --> 00:44:24,300
- Whoa, whoa!
- Ow!

1291
00:44:25,600 --> 00:44:28,910
♫The D Dorm, meet me at the D Dorm♫

1292
00:44:29,200 --> 00:44:32,900
♫The D Dorm, meet me at the D Dorm♫

1293
00:44:35,410 --> 00:44:40,910
♫Every step we take has a meaning♫

1294
00:44:42,690 --> 00:44:47,390
♫No path is ever meaningless♫

1295
00:44:49,840 --> 00:44:55,980
♫As long as our hearts keep searching♫

1296
00:44:56,920 --> 00:45:01,490
♫One day, we'll find
what we're yearning for♫

1297
00:45:01,510 --> 00:45:05,020
♫Walking alone is fine,
but it's better when you're by my side♫

1298
00:45:05,040 --> 00:45:08,620
♫It won't be lonely
when you're here to walk beside♫

1299
00:45:08,640 --> 00:45:12,160
♫Like a love that waits, waits at the D Dorm♫

1300
00:45:12,180 --> 00:45:14,530
♫Like a love that remains,
remains at the dorm♫

1301
00:45:14,560 --> 00:45:20,880
♫Meaningful love and good things
await on every path♫

1302
00:45:21,540 --> 00:45:28,270
♫It might not be a coincidence
that we get to meet♫

1303
00:45:28,750 --> 00:45:35,900
♫There might be hidden meanings
on the path beneath our feet♫

1304
00:45:35,920 --> 00:45:42,840
♫Perhaps the D Dorm
is what led me to meet you♫

1305
00:45:42,860 --> 00:45:46,680
[The D Dorm]
